body:
Scaffold refresh: the first half of `kalide upgrade`. Kalide-owned scaffold content is the content kalide itself writes into a project and still owns — the two author-guide pairs (the deck pair at a project root, agent-authoring, and the library pair at a library root, library-agent-guide; each pair is a full `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` guide plus a short `AGENTS.md` pointer, agent-guide-reference) and the minimal `kalide init` seed tree (cli-init-minimal-seed: the seed `templates/library.yaml`, the `hello` slide template with its `example.md`, the seed default theme `templates/themes/default/theme.css`, and the starter slide `slides/1-hello.md`). The scaffolding commands write this content once and write the full guide only when `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is absent, so a project scaffolded by an older kalide carries that release's guide files. The build-time agent-guide-drift-check keeps each embedded guide in step with the format the code implements — the reserved `media:`/`theme:<name>/` theme-CSS prefixes, the library-wide CSS reach (theme-media-references) and `{{ template }}` layout composition (guide-layout-composition) are carried by the guides — and upgrade is the runtime counterpart of that check.

A refresh member is rewritten only when it is present and byte-identical to a known released kalide version of that same file (global.constraint.upgrade-known-version-catalog). The full guide `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is the one exception: it is also written when absent, because a missing guide is exactly the drift this feature exists to fix and the guide is inert documentation. The pointer file `AGENTS.md` is brought to the agent-guide-reference scheme:
- absent: it is created carrying the reference line `Kalide Reference: ./AGENTS_KALIDE.md` (with a short header), and a missing `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is written with it;
- present and byte-identical to a known released full guide (a pre-scheme release of either guide): it is migrated — `AGENTS.md` is replaced by the short reference file and a new `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is written with the current full guide;
- present and already containing the reference string `Kalide Reference: ./AGENTS_KALIDE.md`: it is left byte-for-byte untouched;
- otherwise (an author `AGENTS.md` without the string): the reference line is appended and the author's existing content is byte-preserved.
The reference append (and the known-full-guide migration) is the one permitted modification of an existing `AGENTS.md` (agent-guide-reference, global.constraint.upgrade-never-clobbers). Seed starter content — the seed `templates/library.yaml`, the `hello` template under `templates/slides/hello/`, the seed default theme `templates/themes/default/theme.css` and the starter slide `slides/1-hello.md`, plus a library's seeded `themes/default/theme.css` — is never re-created when it is absent: an author who deleted it after init has that deletion respected, and upgrade must never introduce a new starter file that would change the deck. A present file whose bytes match no known released version — because the author edited it, or because it is not a kalide scaffold file — is treated as author content: it is left byte-for-byte untouched and reported, never overwritten, whatever the format migration would otherwise do.

The set is scoped to the project's scaffold form and never grows. Which deck owns the seed tree is an objective predicate, not a marker: a deck is a no-arg seed deck exactly when its `kalide.yaml` carries no non-empty `templates:` key (deck.TemplatesPath(cfg) is "") and a local `<deck root>/templates` directory exists. A deck whose `templates:` key is non-empty is an external-library deck; when such a deck also has a local `templates/` directory, that directory is a library layer loaded alongside the external library into the deck's one library (layered-template-library), and upgrade treats it as author content, never as the seed tree. Only a no-arg seed deck owns the seed tree, and the seed-owned paths are exactly `templates/library.yaml`, `templates/slides/hello/*`, `templates/themes/default/theme.css` and `slides/1-hello.md`; an external-library deck's local `templates/` layer is author content, so upgrade never creates a local `templates/` or a starter slide that the deck does not already have, and a library owns its library-root guide pair and its seeded default theme, never templates or media. `kalide.yaml` is the deck config the author edits (title, author, date, properties) and is not a whole-file refresh candidate; its structure is migration territory, not refresh territory. Every refreshed, every migrated, every appended, and every left-alone path is reported.

AC:
- a deck scaffolded by a previous kalide with an unmodified old full guide ends with the current `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` after upgrade, its old `AGENTS.md` full guide replaced by the short reference file, and the project still serves (agent-authoring, agent-guide-reference);
- a full guide `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` that is absent from a deck or library is written; an author-edited `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is left byte-for-byte unchanged and reported;
- an `AGENTS.md` that is absent is created carrying the reference; an author `AGENTS.md` without the reference string gains the appended reference line with all other bytes preserved, and is reported; an `AGENTS.md` already carrying the string is left untouched;
- a deleted starter slide (`slides/1-hello.md`), a deleted `hello` template (`templates/slides/hello/`) and a deleted seed default theme (`templates/themes/default/theme.css`) are not re-created, and a deck the author left valid still serves with identical rendered output before and after upgrade;
- an external-library deck is not given a local `templates/` directory or a starter slide it never had;
- a seed file that is present and byte-identical to a known released version is refreshed to the current content; the same file once the author has edited it is left untouched and reported;
- author slides, sections, templates, themes and media are byte-for-byte identical before and after;
- the command output lists every refreshed path, every migrated/appended path and every path left alone.
